@JobApplication.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5018

### ===========================================================================
###  JobApplication API — Day 3 test suite
### ===========================================================================
###  How to use:
###   1) Start the API (the https profile serves Scalar at /scalar)
###   2) Click "Send Request" on each request, top to bottom
###   3) Tokens are captured automatically from the responses (via @name)
### ===========================================================================


### ===========================================================================
###  1) AUTH — Register
### ===========================================================================

# @name registerRecruiter
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ahmed Recruiter",
  "email": "recruiter@test.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123",
  "role": "Recruiter"
}

### Expected: 201 Created + token

# @name registerCandidate
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mona Candidate",
  "email": "candidate@test.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123",
  "role": "Candidate",
  "cvUrl": "https://example.com/mona-cv.pdf"
}

### Expected: 201 Created + token

# @name registerCandidate2
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sara Candidate",
  "email": "candidate2@test.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123",
  "role": "Candidate"
}

### Expected: 201 Created — a second candidate, used for ownership tests

### --- Error case: duplicate email ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate",
  "email": "candidate@test.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123",
  "role": "Candidate"
}

### Expected: 409 Conflict

### --- Error case: invalid role ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Role",
  "email": "bad@test.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123",
  "role": "Admin"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request

### --- Error case: password too short (validation) ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Short Pass",
  "email": "short@test.com",
  "password": "123",
  "role": "Candidate"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request (model validation)


### ===========================================================================
###  2) AUTH — Login
### ===========================================================================

# @name loginRecruiter
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "recruiter@test.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123",
  "role": "Recruiter"
}

### Expected: 200 OK + token

# @name loginCandidate
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "candidate@test.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123",
  "role": "Candidate"
}

# @name loginCandidate2
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "candidate2@test.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123",
  "role": "Candidate"
}

### Expected: 200 OK

### --- Error case: wrong password ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "candidate@test.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword123"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized — with exactly the same message as the
### "email not found" case below (prevents user enumeration)

### --- Error case: email does not exist ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@test.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized — exactly the same message


### ===========================================================================
###  3) JOBS — Create a job (Recruiter only)
### ===========================================================================

# @name createJob
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "title": "Senior .NET Backend Developer",
  "description": "Seeking a backend developer with 5 years of experience in ASP.NET Core, EF Core, and Clean Architecture."
}

### Expected: 201 Created + { id, title, isActive: true, recruiterId, ... }
### Note the id — it is needed below. If the id is not 1, update the
### hard-coded values underneath.
@jobId = 1

### --- Error case: no token ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should Fail",
  "description": "There is no token at all, so this must be rejected."
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

### --- Error case: candidate token (wrong role) ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "title": "Should Fail",
  "description": "A candidate is not allowed to create a job."
}

### Expected: 403 Forbidden

### --- Error case: empty title (validation) ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "This description is long enough to pass validation."
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request


### ===========================================================================
###  4) APPLICATIONS — Apply for a job (Candidate only)
### ===========================================================================

# @name applyMona
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "jobId": {{jobId}}
}

### Expected: 201 Created
### { id, jobId, candidateId, status: "Applied", appliedAt, statusUpdatedAt, cancelledAt: null }
### Note: there is no candidateId in the request — the system took it from the token.

# @name applySara
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate2.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "jobId": {{jobId}}
}

### Expected: 201 Created — a different candidateId

### --- Error case: duplicate application by the same candidate ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "jobId": {{jobId}}
}

### Expected: 409 Conflict

### --- Error case: job does not exist ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "jobId": 999999
}

### Expected: 404 Not Found

### --- Error case: recruiter token (wrong role) ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "jobId": {{jobId}}
}

### Expected: 403 Forbidden

### --- Error case: JobId = 0 (validation) ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "jobId": 0
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request


### ===========================================================================
###  5) APPLICATIONS — Update status (must own the job)
### ===========================================================================

@applicationId = 1

### --- Applied -> UnderReview (valid transition) ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{applicationId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "UnderReview"
}

### Expected: 204 No Content

### --- UnderReview -> Applied (backwards — forbidden) ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{applicationId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "Applied"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request (forward-only)

### --- UnderReview -> Accepted (skipping a stage — forbidden) ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{applicationId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "Accepted"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request

### --- UnderReview -> InterView (valid) ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{applicationId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "InterView"
}

### Expected: 204 No Content

### --- InterView -> Accepted (valid) ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{applicationId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "Accepted"
}

### Expected: 204 No Content

### --- Accepted -> anything (terminal state — forbidden) ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{applicationId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "Rejected"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request

### --- Error case: application does not exist ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/999999/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "UnderReview"
}

### Expected: 404 Not Found

### --- Error case: wrong role (Candidate) ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{applicationId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "UnderReview"
}

### Expected: 403 Forbidden

### --- Error case: unknown status value ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{applicationId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "NotARealStatus"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request (JSON deserialization)


### ===========================================================================
###  6) APPLICATIONS — Cancel (soft delete, applicant only)
### ===========================================================================
###  Note: use applicationId = 2 (Sara's) because the first one is already
###  Accepted. Adjust the number to match what you actually got.

@cancelTargetId = 2

### --- The applicant cancels while in the Applied state (allowed) ---
DELETE {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{cancelTargetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate2.response.body.$.token}}

### Expected: 204 No Content

### --- Cancelling the same application again (already cancelled) ---
DELETE {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{cancelTargetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate2.response.body.$.token}}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request — Cancelled is not a cancellable state

### --- Someone else tries to cancel an application they do not own (IDOR) ---
DELETE {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{cancelTargetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate.response.body.$.token}}

### Expected: 403 Forbidden

### --- Application does not exist ---
DELETE {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate.response.body.$.token}}

### Expected: 404 Not Found

### --- Recruiter token (wrong role) ---
DELETE {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications/{{cancelTargetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

### Expected: 403 Forbidden


### ===========================================================================
###  7) JOBS — Close a job (owner only)
### ===========================================================================

### --- The owner closes the job ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/jobs/{{jobId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

### Expected: 204 No Content

### --- Closing the same job again (already closed) ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/jobs/{{jobId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request

### --- Job does not exist ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/jobs/999999/close
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRecruiter.response.body.$.token}}

### Expected: 404 Not Found

### --- No token ---
PUT {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/jobs/{{jobId}}/close

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

### --- Applying for a closed job (after closing it above) ---
POST {{JobApplication.API_HostAddress}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCandidate.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "jobId": {{jobId}}
}

### Expected: either 400 Bad Request (the job is closed) or 409 Conflict if
### the candidate had not applied yet. The service checks IsActive before the
### duplicate rule, and this candidate has already applied, so 400 is expected.


### ===========================================================================
###  Important notes
### ===========================================================================
###
### WARNING: to test the "recruiter does not own the job" scenario you need a
###    second recruiter. Register one with a different email, then try closing
###    the job or updating an application status with that token — expect 403.
###
### WARNING: the id values (jobId / applicationId) are hard-coded here because
###    an .http file has limited support for dynamic variables. Read the real
###    values from the responses and adjust them.
###
### WARNING: this .http file is a manual test harness — it is not part of the
###    application itself.
